Removing the `DocumentStatus.PENDING` guard at lines 108–110 lets execution continue into the remaining field-level checks and ultimately into the transaction writes. Behavioral effects depend on the remaining checks passing; sole enforcement across unread helpers and middleware remains **unverified**.

**Verified call paths and conditions**

**`field-router/router.ts` — `signFieldWithToken` procedure (lines 615–633)**

```
615:633:packages/trpc/server/field-router/router.ts
  signFieldWithToken: procedure.input(ZSignFieldWithTokenMutationSchema).mutation(async ({ input, ctx }) => {
    const { token, fieldId, value, isBase64, authOptions } = input;

    ctx.logger.info({
      input: {
        fieldId,
      },
    });

    return await signFieldWithToken({
      token,
      fieldId,
      value: value ?? '',
      isBase64,
      userId: ctx.user?.id,
      authOptions,
      requestMetadata: ctx.metadata.requestMetadata,
    });
  }),
```

This route uses bare `procedure` (not `authenticatedProcedure`) and passes `ctx.user?.id` as optional. No document status is checked before the call. If the PENDING guard is dropped, this route becomes the direct path for signing fields on envelopes in any status the database holds.

**`apply-multi-sign-signature.ts` — loop call (lines 74–84)**

